From: CrashSystemZ <100166199+CrashSystemZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:28:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Don't load the OpenGL driver to list GPUs without
 EGL.

lock_display_devices() asks get_opengl_gpus() for the GPUs OpenGL knows, and that loads the
whole OpenGL driver first. Only EGL devices are listed, though, so a build without EGL (every
macOS build) always gets an empty list. On macOS loading the driver means its pixel formats and
a first GL context under Rosetta: 610 ms in explorer.exe /desktop on every cold start of a
prefix, with every program waiting for the desktop meanwhile.

Without EGL, return no OpenGL GPUs straight away. A program that uses OpenGL still loads the
driver itself, when it first needs it.

Original work for Hamster Launcher (LGPL-2.1-or-later).

Topic: desktop-start
---
 dlls/win32u/opengl.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/opengl.c b/dlls/win32u/opengl.c
--- a/dlls/win32u/opengl.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/opengl.c
@@ -3378,6 +3378,13 @@ BOOL get_opengl_gpus( struct list *gpus )
 {
     struct egl_platform *egl;
 
+#ifndef SONAME_LIBEGL
+    /* Only EGL devices are listed, so without EGL the list is always empty: don't initialize the
+     * OpenGL driver just to find that out. On macOS that is its pixel formats and a first context,
+     * ~0.6 s in the desktop process, which every program of a cold prefix waits for. */
+    return FALSE;
+#endif
+
     if (!__wine_get_opengl_driver( WINE_OPENGL_DRIVER_VERSION )) return FALSE;
 
     LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY( egl, &devices_egl, struct egl_platform, entry )
